d, timestamp, and nested payload objects were not mutated.\n\n**Private/edge tests:**\n\n- Whitespace-only `correctsEventId`, malformed timestamp, non-object payload, unsupported type, and absent complete-payload fields.\n- Same correction ID with different content.\n- Concurrent submissions of the same correction.\n- A permitted correction chain and rejection of correction against a superseded/non-active target if that is the chosen rule.\n- Publisher mutation of its argument does not alter audit or active state.\n- Returned store objects are defensive clones.\n- Replay after a publish failure and replay after full success produce the frozen status semantics.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nFirst freeze correction semantics: especially what event may be targeted, whether chains are allowed, what constitutes a complete replacement, and whether acceptance is distinct from successful publication. Then update normalization, add an atomic store operation that appends the correction and supersedes its target, expose separate audit and active queries, update routing and retryable publication handling, and finally add the focused tests above.\n\nThe most important decision to freeze before coding is the atomic state/publication contract: when a correction becomes active and how a persisted correction is safely republished after publication failure without applying it twice."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"openai/gpt-5.6-sol","usage":{"input":3,"output":1504,"cacheRead":1668,"cacheWrite":1106,"reasoning":183,"totalTokens":4281,"cost":{"input":0.000007500000000000001,"output":0.02256,"cacheRead":0.000417,"cacheWrite":0.00345625,"total":0.026440750000000002}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1787542529600,"responseId":"gen-1787542529-e44p1x8FAEKRcL6JrnkM","rawStopReason":"stop"}}
